---
import Doc from '../layouts/Doc.astro';
import SiteLink from '../components/SiteLink.astro';
import { APP_NAME, BUSINESS_NAME, SUPPORT_EMAIL } from '../utils/env';

const effectiveDateISO = '2026-08-29';
const effectiveDateLabel = 'August 29, 2026';
---

<Doc
  title="Privacy"
  description={`How ${APP_NAME} handles data.`}
>
  <header class="doc__header">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
  </header>

  <p>We are {BUSINESS_NAME}, the publisher of {APP_NAME}.</p>

  <section>
    <h2>Game data</h2>
    <p>
      The drawings you send as game messages go through Messages, not to us.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      We use <SiteLink href="https://telemetrydeck.com/privacy/" target="_blank" aria-label="TelemetryDeck privacy policy, opens in new tab">TelemetryDeck</SiteLink> to understand how {APP_NAME} is used and to
      improve the app. The app sends information about app use, purchases,
      crashes, performance, and app, device, and settings details, including
      accessibility settings. It also sends a one-way hash of a random ID made
      for that installation. The ID stays the same until the app's data is
      reset or the app is uninstalled.
    </p>
    <p>
      Analytics records do not include your name or email address. You can stop
      future analytics in the app's settings. This does not remove information
      already sent. We do not set a fixed deletion date for past analytics.
      Because we cannot connect those records to your name or email address, we
      cannot find and delete one person's analytics.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Content reports</h2>
    <p>
      If you send us a content report, the email includes your reason, the
      round ID, app version, and build number. The report comes from your email
      account, so we receive that email address. A drawing is included only if
      you choose to attach it.
    </p>
    <p>
      We keep report emails in our support inbox. You can ask us to remove your
      report from that inbox by emailing <SiteLink href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</SiteLink> from the same address used to send it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy as {APP_NAME} changes. Questions about this
      policy can be sent to <SiteLink href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</SiteLink>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <footer class="doc__meta">Effective <time datetime={effectiveDateISO}>{effectiveDateLabel}</time></footer>
</Doc>
